  "final_observations": [
    "The fixed three-epoch row method did not exceed the matrix baseline on validation macro accuracy.",
    "Extending fixed warm-up to five epochs increased assignment stability and KS-ER pair prevalence but decreased validation macro accuracy, especially ER accuracy. More stable assignments were not automatically better predictions.",
    "Adaptive warm-up stopped after four epochs because 94.05% and 95.00% of proposed row pairs remained unchanged over two consecutive eligible transitions. All-row sharing then began in epoch five.",
    "The adaptive all-row run is the leading single run on both validation macro and validation overall accuracy, and its validation-selected test result is also the strongest among these five runs.",
    "Confidence gating at a 10% relative margin kept 756 rows independent but reduced validation macro accuracy relative to adaptive all-row sharing. This threshold is not supported as a replacement by the current evidence.",
    "The gated run's declining post-freeze match rate is not assignment drift or a code failure. It reflects independent rows changing their current closest pair while frozen decisions remain fixed."
  ],
  "decision": {
    "best_current_single_run": "row_adaptive_all",
    "keep_as_strong_baseline": "matrix",
    "do_not_promote": ["row_fixed_3", "row_fixed_5", "row_adaptive_gate_0p10"],
    "next_step": "Confirm adaptive all-row sharing versus matrix sharing on additional controlled seeds before claiming a robust gain. Do not tune more confidence thresholds using the test set.",
    "caveats": [
      "Each method has only one run here; the adaptive-all advantage over matrix is small and may vary by seed.",
      "The adaptive ungated and gated runs used different GPU indices, which can introduce small nondeterministic differences despite matching seed and pre-sharing assignments.",
      "Validation ER contains only 553 samples, so small changes in correct predictions visibly affect its accuracy.",
      "All test comparisons use the checkpoint selected by validation macro accuracy, not the test-best checkpoint.",
      "These are separate row-sharing methodology ablations, not the original whole-matrix NCMTL algorithm."
    ]
  }
